> 4. In general when you find lots of armor should you don whatever you
> can? Like +0 elven cloak, a black cap (+0 something else etc.), or
> just stick to your best armor only. 

Personally I figure out what is blessed/uncursed/cursed then wear all the
uncursed/blessed stuff at least once to get the +0/+2/+3 info then
stow the least protective and wear the rest.  You can wear armor, helmets,
gloves, cloaks/coats, boots/shoes and shields.  Maybe more I have only
recently got to level 8.

> 5. Should you just sell all extra stuff to shopkeepers?

If you carry all that stuff arround you will use up food and might not
be able to carry something you need.  I find a good place to put a 
large box and then fill it up with all the stuff I collect.  I comes
in handy when I manage to get my armor destroyed to go to the closet
and get a new shield that I know is safe.  It also keeps monsters from
picking up a weapon I left around and hitting me with it.

> 6. In general should you steal from a shopkeeper? THe only way I can
> think of is to dig a trap door, but doesn't that abandon your pet at
> that level (or will he fall down with you if he is next to you when
> you begin digging)? In general, I have found it better to just wait
> till my pet fleeces most everything from the shop (I pick it all up
> and keep it handy near the door).
> 
I just train my pet for the stuff in the shops.  That way I don't need so 
much money.  Also waiting around for my pet lets me gain experience levels 
fighting off the stuff that comes to kill me cause I didn't leave the level.

